      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T18:40:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch, it was wrong interpretation on my side: 32 is the maximum raw iMCU height, but converted output can include one deferred interpolation group in addition to the regular eight groups. With the maximum vertical sampling factor of 4, zune-jpeg’s direct stripe threshold is `(8 + 1) * 4 \u003d 36 rows`.\n\nUsing 32 is correct but would force zune-jpeg through its internal staging path for `maxV\u003d4` images. I’ll increase the C++ batch size to 36, update the comment, and adjust the buffer-size test bound accordingly.",
      "parentUuid": "6b43d7e7_94557c2a",
